WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.800 --> 00:00:02.067
Faithfulness scoring.

2
00:00:02.367 --> 00:00:07.700
This is the hallucination check for RAG, and the metric enterprise buyers ask about first.

3
00:00:08.900 --> 00:00:13.933
Faithfulness asks: is every claim in the answer supported by the retrieved context?

4
00:00:14.233 --> 00:00:16.267
First, take the generated answer.

5
00:00:16.567 --> 00:00:18.633
Decompose it into atomic claims.

6
00:00:18.933 --> 00:00:23.200
An LLM judge checks each claim against the context, yes or no.

7
00:00:23.500 --> 00:00:25.631
The score is the supported fraction.

8
00:00:25.631 --> 00:00:30.367
An unsupported claim is something the model made up or dragged in from training.

9
00:00:31.567 --> 00:00:33.067
Be clear about its limits.

10
00:00:33.367 --> 00:00:36.680
It checks that every claim traces back to the context.

11
00:00:36.680 --> 00:00:42.078
It does not check correctness or completeness, because the context itself could be thin.

12
00:00:42.078 --> 00:00:43.367
That is recall's job.

13
00:00:43.667 --> 00:00:47.026
Nor does it check whether the answer addresses the question.

14
00:00:47.026 --> 00:00:48.033
That is relevancy.

15
00:00:48.333 --> 00:00:51.467
Faithfulness does one thing: no claim without a source.

16
00:00:52.667 --> 00:00:54.200
Here is the idea in code.

17
00:00:54.500 --> 00:00:56.900
One prompt lists the claims, one per line.

18
00:00:57.200 --> 00:01:01.326
Another asks, for each claim, whether the context fully supports it.

19
00:01:01.326 --> 00:01:01.933
Yes or no.

20
00:01:02.233 --> 00:01:04.662
The score is the fraction of yes answers.

21
00:01:04.662 --> 00:01:09.933
Do this by hand once for one answer, and you will understand the automated score forever.

22
00:01:11.133 --> 00:01:15.267
Here is a Mission Control answer about the Apollo 13 review board.

23
00:01:15.567 --> 00:01:18.664
Faithfulness flags it at zero point seven five.

24
00:01:18.664 --> 00:01:21.233
Three claims are supported, one is not.

25
00:01:21.533 --> 00:01:24.606
The panel concluded schedule pressure was a factor.

26
00:01:24.606 --> 00:01:27.800
That sentence exists nowhere in the retrieved chunks.

27
00:01:29.000 --> 00:01:30.600
The answer reads beautifully.

28
00:01:30.900 --> 00:01:34.867
But the model imported a plausible sounding conclusion from its pretraining.

29
00:01:35.167 --> 00:01:40.891
For a compliance customer, citing a finding that isn't in their documents is the nightmare.

30
00:01:40.891 --> 00:01:43.533
Faithfulness catches it on every eval run.

31
00:01:44.733 --> 00:01:45.492
Let's recap.

32
00:01:45.492 --> 00:01:48.400
Faithfulness asks if every claim is supported.

33
00:01:48.700 --> 00:01:51.367
Split into claims, verify each, and score.

34
00:01:51.667 --> 00:01:53.867
It is the hallucination check for RAG.

35
00:01:54.167 --> 00:01:57.191
But it doesn't judge correctness or relevance.

36
00:01:57.191 --> 00:01:58.900
Next up: answer relevancy.
